Conditions accept `bool` values and numeric values. `0` is false; everything else is true.

`write` prints without a trailing newline. `writeln` prints a value followed by a newline.

```redb
@include "std"

main() {
    write("loading")
    write("...")
    writeln("")
    writeln("done")
}
```

